From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 19:17:22 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] media: i2c: lc898123f40: defer probe until the controller
 answers

At boot the controller does not ACK until the IMX362 driver has brought up
the camera module rails, so probing first failed with -ENXIO ("controller
not ready") on every boot, while binding the same device later always
worked (firmware 0x19, stabilisation on).

Poll for a boot window and defer the probe instead of failing; deferred
probes rerun when the sensor binds. Which module rail the part needs is not
established yet, so the dependency cannot be described in the binding.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
---
 drivers/media/i2c/lc898123f40.c | 21 +++++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/i2c/lc898123f40.c b/drivers/media/i2c/lc898123f40.c
index f85c9b54c1e6..7e96ab9614cb 100644
--- a/drivers/media/i2c/lc898123f40.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/lc898123f40.c
@@ -42,6 +42,7 @@
  */
 
 #include <linux/i2c.h>
+#include <linux/iopoll.h>
 #include <linux/module.h>
 #include <linux/mutex.h>
 #include <linux/nvmem-provider.h>
@@ -159,7 +160,7 @@ static int lc898123f40_probe(struct i2c_client *client)
 	};
 	struct lc898123f40 *ois;
 	unsigned int fw;
-	int ret;
+	int ret, err;
 
 	ois = devm_kzalloc(dev, sizeof(*ois), GFP_KERNEL);
 	if (!ois)
@@ -178,10 +179,22 @@ static int lc898123f40_probe(struct i2c_client *client)
 	if (IS_ERR(ois->regmap))
 		return PTR_ERR(ois->regmap);
 
-	/* the firmware boots from flash; a command completes once it is up */
-	ret = lc898123f40_wait_ready(ois);
+	/*
+	 * The firmware boots from flash; a command completes once it is up.
+	 * Until then the part does not even ACK, and at boot it stays silent
+	 * until the IMX362 driver has brought its own rails up: probing after
+	 * that works every time, probing first never does. Which of those
+	 * rails it needs is not established, so wait for a boot window and
+	 * then defer rather than fail -- deferred probes rerun when the sensor
+	 * binds.
+	 * ponytail: deferral stands in for the missing supply; name that rail
+	 * in the binding once it is found and this becomes a plain failure.
+	 */
+	ret = read_poll_timeout(lc898123f40_wait_ready, err, !err, 10000,
+				200000, false, ois);
 	if (ret)
-		return dev_err_probe(dev, ret, "controller not ready\n");
+		return dev_err_probe(dev, -EPROBE_DEFER,
+				     "controller not answering (%d)\n", err);
 
 	ret = regmap_read(ois->regmap, LC898123F40_REG_FW_VERSION, &fw);
 	if (ret)
